<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Houthi movement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1990s–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Ansar Allah, Houthis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Houthi movement, officially Ansar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a>, is a Zaydi Shia political and armed movement from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saada">Saada</a> region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, named after its founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-badreddin-al-houthi">Hussein Badreddin al-Houthi</a>. After six wars with the government from 2004 to 2010, it seized Sanaa in September 2014 with help from forces loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-abdullah-saleh">Ali Abdullah Saleh</a>, and it has since ruled most of the populous north, backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/houthi-movement.jpg" alt="Houthi movement" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RuneAgerhus · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Slogan_of_the_Houthi_Movement.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
